  "decision": "Raised the $5K estimate one point to 62% and held the $10K estimate at 31%. ETH's 5.1% rally to about $2.73K, higher volume, lower oil, and a U.S. 10-year yield below 5% modestly improved the path toward $3K, but the move was broad-market and did not confirm a new ETH valuation regime. The ECB's Pontes launch strengthens the institutional-tokenization signal while remaining blockchain-neutral. ETF data for September 21 was incomplete, and high yields plus meaningful odds of another Fed hike keep cyclical liquidity red; this remains separate from the unchanged structural debasement thesis. Ethereum L1 revenue remained small relative to application fees, so the explicit ETH value-capture penalty keeps the $10K probability unchanged. No catalyst crossed a color threshold and no thesis-breaking event occurred."
